Subject: Input: Size the evdev buffer for EV_BTN buttons

input_estimate_events_per_packet() makes room for "KEY and MSC events" with a
constant 7, and evdev sizes a client's buffer as 8 packets of that estimate,
rounded up to a power of two. A device with 128 buttons that changes many of
them in one report sends one EV_BTN event per changed button plus the EV_KEY
and MSC_SCAN events of the first 80, more than the buffer holds: the 128-button
fixture pressing all buttons at once delivered 44 of 128 EV_BTN events and a
SYN_DROPPED. Add one event per button when the device has EV_BTN.

[ORDER 15: not part of Tomasz Pakuła's posted series; found by the runtime proof of the series on a
reduced 7.3.1 kernel (report of milestone 2), proposed to the author with its test. Drop it if his next
version sizes the buffer itself.]
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
 drivers/input/input.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/input.c b/drivers/input/input.c
--- a/drivers/input/input.c
+++ b/drivers/input/input.c
@@ -2236,6 +2236,10 @@
 	/* Make room for KEY and MSC events */
 	events += 7;
 
+	/* Every generic button can change in one report */
+	if (test_bit(EV_BTN, dev->evbit))
+		events += dev->button_count;
+
 	return events;
 }
 
